# Virtue of Strength {5}{G}{G}: "If you tap a basic land for mana, it produces three times as much of that mana instead" (CR 614.1a,
# 106.12b, 205.4a). Turn 1 Bot1 casts it with Black Lotus (GGG) and four Moxen. Turn 3 Bot1 plays a Forest and taps it: {G}{G}{G}; Mox
# Emerald, an artifact, still adds one {G} (not a land); the pool is {G}x4. Turn 5 Bot1 plays Taiga, a nonbasic land with two basic land
# types, and taps it for {R}: one {R}, not tripled, because it lacks the basic supertype.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Virtue of Strength
Forest
Taiga
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
